---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';

const ids = ['harnesses.claudeCode.askForEvidence', 't3code.htmlRenders', 't3code.browser'];
const prompt = `When you finish, hand back proof I can judge in a minute, before you say done:
- a screenshot of every page you changed, at phone width (390 pixels) and desktop width
- the test command you ran and its full output
- for any number the change affects: its value before and after
- a short list of what you did not check, and why
If something could not be checked, say so instead of guessing.`;
---
<Journey chapter="proof" first="word" title="Proof you can read" description="An agent can hand back more than the word done: a summary, a test run, a screenshot, and a link to try. Each catches a different kind of miss at a glance.">
  <Step id="word" title="“Done” is only one word">
    <p><a href={url('journey/check/')}>The check from step 5</a> only says pass or fail. When it passes, all you get back is “Done.”—leaving you to read 212 changed lines yourself to verify the agent actually built what you asked for.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="cards" title="Ask for proof alongside the work">
    <p>Ask the agent to place four proof cards on your tray: a short summary, the test output, a screenshot, and a link to try it.</p>
    <p>Automated checks tell you pass or fail; proof cards let you judge the result at a glance.</p>
    <More title="Where this comes from">
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.askForEvidence" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="catch" title="Each card catches a different kind of miss">
    <p>All six example tasks pass the automated check, yet four miss what you actually wanted. Each proof card flags a different miss in orange—turn any card off and watch that kind of mistake slip through as “done”.</p>
    <div class="pick" data-multi role="group" aria-label="Proof cards that are switched on">
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="sum" data-default aria-pressed="true">Summary</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="tests" data-default aria-pressed="true">Test run</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="shot" data-default aria-pressed="true">Screenshot</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="link" data-default aria-pressed="true">Link</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A worked check for a number">
      <dl>
        <dt>Reference</dt><dd>Fees paid last season, from the club’s spreadsheet: €14,880 (illustrative).</dd>
        <dt>Tolerance</dt><dd>For money, exact match. For a measured value, write down the allowed margin before the run.</dd>
        <dt>Rerun</dt><dd>The agent runs the calculation again on a fresh copy of the data and gets the same result.</dd>
        <dt>The card</dt><dd>“Total €14,880.00. Reference €14,880.00. Rerun €14,880.00. Match.”</dd>
      </dl>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="during" title="See progress while it runs">
    <p>On a longer task, ask the agent to update a live progress card on your tray as it goes. When it veers off-script at step 4 into work you never asked for, you spot it immediately without interrupting the run.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="progress" data-val="on" data-default aria-pressed="true">A progress file</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="progress" data-val="off" aria-pressed="false">Nothing until the end</button>
    </div>
    <More title="In T3 Code">
      <p><Fact id="t3code.htmlRenders" show="claim" /> <Fact id="t3code.browser" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="ask" title="Match the proof to the job">
    <p>Tell the agent upfront what evidence fits the task: phone and desktop screenshots for a page, sample rows before and after for a script, or a failing test turned passing for a bug fix.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="kind" data-val="page" data-default aria-pressed="true">A page</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="kind" data-val="script" aria-pressed="false">A script</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="kind" data-val="fix" aria-pressed="false">A bug fix</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt title="Proof with the work" compact>{prompt}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
    <Next from="proof" more={[{ href: 'explain/verification/', text: 'Checking the work' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The example tasks, the 212 changed lines, the sample counts, and the planted misses are illustrative.</p>
    <Verified ids={ids} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
